1
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,500
Which part do you need me to explain?

2
00:01:57,890 --> 00:01:59,420
From the start.

3
00:02:10,970 --> 00:02:13,060
Everyone knows by now...

4
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:14,700
that you're with that woman.

5
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:16,460
I'm here to beg you.

6
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:18,860
Please, ask for Bu-nga’s hand for me.

7
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:21,820
She will never be my daughter-in-law.

8
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:23,340
Hello?

9
00:02:24,170 --> 00:02:25,980
- Ploy.
- Can you hear me?

10
00:02:28,370 --> 00:02:29,420
Is the signal bad?

11
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:30,660
Yeah.

12
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:32,740
I hear music in the background.

13
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:34,220
It’s a Nora song.

14
00:02:35,610 --> 00:02:36,820
What did you say?

15
00:02:37,370 --> 00:02:38,660
Are you looking for someone?

16
00:02:38,890 --> 00:02:40,420
I'm here for the fortune teller.

17
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:41,620
Wait here.

18
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:44,660
I had a weird dream.

19
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,020
I've never had a dream like that before.

20
00:02:48,050 --> 00:02:49,620
It was about a woman.

21
00:02:50,610 --> 00:02:51,820
Could she be the owner?

22
00:02:52,050 --> 00:02:55,460
Persevere in your righteous deeds.

23
00:02:55,770 --> 00:02:59,740
To shield your life from certain death.

24
00:03:00,970 --> 00:03:02,740
I hope it's not too late.

25
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:37,580
Chanchao!

26
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:43,260
Ploy, watch out!

27
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,220
...do the right thing.

28
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,460
No one is going anywhere.

29
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,500
Including my wife.

30
00:03:57,940 --> 00:03:59,860
She will move in with us.

31
00:04:03,930 --> 00:04:06,180
Once Thep is established,

32
00:04:06,890 --> 00:04:09,020
we’ll hold a proper wedding.

33
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,180
Watch your step.

34
00:04:19,670 --> 00:04:22,380
I'll finish my work quickly and hurry back.

35
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:23,340
Okay.

36
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:26,980
My little one.

37
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:30,580
It’ll just be the two of you today.
Be good for mommy.

38
00:04:31,930 --> 00:04:33,580
You act like the baby can understand.

39
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:34,420
You see,

40
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:36,300
in the West, they say...

41
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:38,900
babies can hear everything in there.

42
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:44,420
Are you ready, Thep?

43
00:04:46,450 --> 00:04:47,380
Yes, Father.

44
00:05:00,290 --> 00:05:01,060
It's time.

45
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:05,820
I must thank you again, Mother...

46
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:08,100
for your kindness.

47
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:11,460
Please take good care of her.

48
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,300
While I'm away,

49
00:05:15,010 --> 00:05:16,700
she can stay in my room.

50
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,300
Please have someone look after her.

51
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,300
Make sure no one is unkind.

52
00:05:27,810 --> 00:05:29,580
Safe travels.

53
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,500
Once you reach Luang Sakorn’s...

54
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,220
send word.

55
00:05:34,890 --> 00:05:35,580
I will.

56
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:40,180
Take care, son.

57
00:05:41,570 --> 00:05:42,460
I'll be going now.

58
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:55,660
Bu-nga

59
00:05:55,970 --> 00:05:56,740
Yes?

60
00:05:57,490 --> 00:05:58,460
It’s time for me to go.

61
00:06:09,650 --> 00:06:10,620
I’m off now.

62
00:06:11,850 --> 00:06:12,860
Okay.

63
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,820
Did you forget something?

64
00:06:36,570 --> 00:06:38,300
May I have a moment, Father?

65
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,380
Bu-nga

66
00:07:19,170 --> 00:07:20,460
I’ll be back soon.

67
00:07:22,330 --> 00:07:25,420
I honestly hate being apart from you.

68
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:30,620
I'm afraid of losing you.

69
00:07:31,370 --> 00:07:32,500
Don’t be.

70
00:07:33,210 --> 00:07:34,620
I'll only love you.

71
00:07:34,810 --> 00:07:35,820
I promise.

72
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:55,140
My, my.

73
00:07:55,450 --> 00:07:58,900
That Bu-nga certainly has a way with men.

74
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:02,300
No wonder
he’s completely head over heels.

75
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:03,940
Quiet.

76
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:04,900
Why?

77
00:08:06,210 --> 00:08:07,060
My Lady!

78
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:21,140
He’s doing this for your family’s future.

79
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,620
It's time to go, Thep.

80
00:08:23,810 --> 00:08:25,940
I’ll look after her.

81
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:28,140
Thank you, Mok.

82
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:52,860
Ouch!

83
00:08:53,290 --> 00:08:54,020
Mok?

84
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:56,380
Oops!

85
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:57,460
Oh, goodness

86
00:08:57,730 --> 00:08:58,780
I'm so sorry.

87
00:09:01,130 --> 00:09:03,940
I was afraid you'd fall,
so I gripped too hard.

88
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:06,220
It's fine.

89
00:09:06,930 --> 00:09:09,300
Let’s head inside.
You might catch a cold.

90
00:09:09,970 --> 00:09:10,740
Okay.

91
00:09:22,610 --> 00:09:23,620
Well...

92
00:09:23,850 --> 00:09:27,820
I wondered how you could accept her.

93
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:31,460
Turns out you have it all planned out.

94
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:37,780
Are you sending her back home?

95
00:09:40,930 --> 00:09:42,740
Thep would surely find out.

96
00:09:43,730 --> 00:09:45,460
Then what is your plan?

97
00:09:56,250 --> 00:09:58,060
The Lady insists you stay here.

98
00:10:01,370 --> 00:10:03,420
But Mr. Thep said she could use his room.

99
00:10:04,090 --> 00:10:07,580
The stairs aren’t safe
for a pregnant woman.

100
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:10,420
Stay here until the baby is born.

101
00:10:11,770 --> 00:10:12,540
Got it.

102
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:15,420
Move it.

103
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:28,020
I'll get you some bedding.

104
00:10:43,330 --> 00:10:45,260
Just stay here for now.

105
00:10:45,570 --> 00:10:48,660
I’ll try to get you moved upstairs.

106
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:51,660
This is more than enough.

107
00:10:52,570 --> 00:10:53,580
Oh, dear...

108
00:10:53,930 --> 00:10:55,660
You’re far too humble.

109
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:59,460
If anyone mistreats you, tell me.

110
00:10:59,930 --> 00:11:02,300
Think of me as your real sister.

111
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:06,580
Thank you.

112
00:11:07,290 --> 00:11:09,100
Without you and Khem,

113
00:11:09,410 --> 00:11:12,580
I wouldn't dare stay here alone.

114
00:11:14,770 --> 00:11:18,060
You have such a strong heart.

115
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:21,820
I couldn't handle it like you.

116
00:11:22,530 --> 00:11:24,820
If I weren't the official wife...

117
00:11:24,970 --> 00:11:27,380
I'd never let my husband go so far.

118
00:11:27,850 --> 00:11:29,780
Especially to the capital.

119
00:11:29,970 --> 00:11:32,580
There are many beautiful women there.

120
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:59,180
Please wait here, Father.

121
00:12:00,170 --> 00:12:01,900
I’ll see if the train has arrived.

122
00:12:36,570 --> 00:12:38,540
The platform is that way.

123
00:12:39,170 --> 00:12:42,540
Can't I enjoy just a little of the view?

124
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:46,460
That wasn't little. You were ogling!

125
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:48,180
Have you no shame?

126
00:12:48,450 --> 00:12:49,380
None at all.

127
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,820
We may only cross paths this once.

128
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,060
My,

129
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:55,380
how feisty!

130
00:12:56,370 --> 00:12:57,460
Come on, let’s go.

131
00:13:20,730 --> 00:13:21,980
Sir! Sir!

132
00:13:22,970 --> 00:13:24,420
Sir! Oh, he fainted!

133
00:13:24,650 --> 00:13:25,780
Someone's collapsed!

134
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,100
Someone's collapsed!

135
00:13:27,570 --> 00:13:28,780
Someone's collapsed!

136
00:13:29,090 --> 00:13:30,340
Someone's collapsed here!

137
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:34,220
Help!

138
00:13:34,650 --> 00:13:36,740
Does anyone have smelling salts?

139
00:13:37,330 --> 00:13:38,420
Are you okay?

140
00:13:38,610 --> 00:13:39,460
Sir?

141
00:13:39,890 --> 00:13:43,860
Stand back, everyone!
Give him some air!

142
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:45,660
- Please step back.
- Sir?

143
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:00,060
Give me the smelling salts.

144
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:10,260
How are you feeling?

145
00:14:19,170 --> 00:14:21,340
Here, take a small sip.

146
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:45,660
Father!

147
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:54,980
Be careful.

148
00:15:05,650 --> 00:15:06,580
How are you feeling?

149
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:38,060
We are midwifery students from Siriraj.

150
00:15:38,650 --> 00:15:40,780
We're taking a trip
to Hua Hin for the holiday.

151
00:15:42,970 --> 00:15:44,620
My father and I are here on business.

152
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:47,980
Until we meet again.

153
00:15:49,210 --> 00:15:50,500
Goodbye.

154
00:16:03,650 --> 00:16:05,860
Until we meet again?

155
00:16:07,010 --> 00:16:08,100
Who said...

156
00:16:08,290 --> 00:16:10,620
we'd only cross paths once?

157
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:13,620
It must be fate.

158
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:27,700
May the Triple Gem and all sacred spirits,

159
00:16:27,890 --> 00:16:30,020
and Jomthap's ancestors,

160
00:16:30,170 --> 00:16:33,740
protect and watch over him.

161
00:16:33,850 --> 00:16:35,940
May he awaken soon.

162
00:16:36,330 --> 00:16:37,980
Amen.

163
00:16:52,410 --> 00:16:53,420
Jomthap!

164
00:16:55,650 --> 00:16:57,380
Can you see me clearly?

165
00:16:58,690 --> 00:16:59,340
Yes.

166
00:16:59,930 --> 00:17:02,980
Can you see everything
around you clearly?

167
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,500
I can. Why do you ask?

168
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:12,140
You hit your head while helping me.

169
00:17:12,330 --> 00:17:14,380
You’ve been out for almost a week.

170
00:17:14,530 --> 00:17:17,460
The doctor feared for your vision...

171
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:20,180
due to the frontal lobe concussion.

172
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:22,060
Ploy...

173
00:17:22,410 --> 00:17:23,420
Don't worry.

174
00:17:23,570 --> 00:17:25,660
Right now, I can see perfectly clearly.

175
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:30,300
But you still need a full exam.

176
00:17:32,810 --> 00:17:33,500
All right.

177
00:17:51,490 --> 00:17:53,140
Is Chanchao with Thep?

178
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:54,580
No.

179
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:58,700
Thep is at work.
I sent her to her tutor.

180
00:17:58,810 --> 00:18:00,660
I'll pick her up this evening.

181
00:18:02,330 --> 00:18:04,580
I've caused your family so much trouble.

182
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:09,660
Don't worry.
Consider us family, too.

183
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,740
Does my mother know I’m in the hospital?

184
00:18:15,050 --> 00:18:15,980
She does.

185
00:18:16,090 --> 00:18:19,820
We needed her consent for the surgery.

186
00:18:19,970 --> 00:18:25,940
She's tied to your stepfather.
She asked us to stay instead.

187
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:29,860
I thought it would be more difficult at first.

188
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:33,020
But once the staff heard your name,

189
00:18:33,130 --> 00:18:35,340
everyone was eager to help.

190
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:41,380
I know my family has deep roots here.

191
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,780
But they've all passed away.

192
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:46,260
I didn't think it still mattered.

193
00:18:47,090 --> 00:18:50,060
Your grandparents are revered here.

194
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:53,060
How so?

195
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:10,540
Lady Duangkhae Dechadireksorn

196
00:19:11,290 --> 00:19:13,980
She donated the land for this hospital.

197
00:19:35,730 --> 00:19:37,660
People in that family don't live long.

198
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,620
None of them make it to 50.

199
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:43,820
It's a curse.

200
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:49,060
Excuse me.

201
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:52,340
Where does a girl named Busaban live?

202
00:20:52,610 --> 00:20:53,500
Busaban?

203
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:56,060
The college student.

204
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,420
No one’s lived here for years.

205
00:21:00,650 --> 00:21:03,820
I only come by for the mail.

206
00:21:04,810 --> 00:21:05,500
Oh,

207
00:21:05,850 --> 00:21:06,860
are you sure?

208
00:21:07,610 --> 00:21:10,900
I remember... I took her here myself.

209
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:12,780
Of course, I'm sure.

210
00:21:13,010 --> 00:21:14,740
I own all these buildings.

211
00:21:14,890 --> 00:21:18,460
They're closed for repairs.
No one’s inside.

212
00:21:41,810 --> 00:21:43,500
Why did you lie about living here?

213
00:21:47,650 --> 00:21:49,180
Where you live is your own business.

214
00:21:50,050 --> 00:21:51,260
But you've not handed in your work.

215
00:22:06,170 --> 00:22:08,300
I’ve told you this class has no exams.

216
00:22:08,610 --> 00:22:10,260
Your grade depends on your assignments.

217
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,620
So, what’s the problem?

218
00:22:17,850 --> 00:22:18,820
Come with me.

219
00:22:20,290 --> 00:22:21,620
Then you'll understand.

220
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:14,020
I don't think anyone lives here.

221
00:23:15,820 --> 00:23:17,780
Wait here. I'll go check.

222
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:21,340
I've been here before.

223
00:23:25,890 --> 00:23:26,860
My home.

224
00:24:44,970 --> 00:24:45,740
Busaban.

225
00:24:47,930 --> 00:24:48,740
Busaban!

226
00:26:03,390 --> 00:26:04,260
There...

227
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:05,380
you are.

228
00:26:18,650 --> 00:26:20,740
I curse every last one of you!

229
00:26:20,990 --> 00:26:23,180
You've stripped me of everything.

230
00:26:23,490 --> 00:26:26,180
May you and your kin perish.

231
00:26:26,530 --> 00:26:28,380
In every lifetime...

232
00:26:28,570 --> 00:26:30,300
I will hunt you down.

233
00:26:30,530 --> 00:26:34,180
Even your souls shall find no refuge in hell.

234
00:26:34,300 --> 00:26:37,220
Be ruined for eternity.

235
00:26:49,050 --> 00:26:50,180
Don't do this.

236
00:26:52,370 --> 00:26:54,020
I understand you.

237
00:26:55,250 --> 00:26:57,100
But you don't have to do this.

238
00:26:58,250 --> 00:27:00,140
I'm a teacher. You're my student.

239
00:27:00,690 --> 00:27:01,820
I'm here to educate you,

240
00:27:02,640 --> 00:27:04,380
not to take advantage of you.

241
00:27:06,280 --> 00:27:08,180
I do understand your struggle.

242
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:10,580
Let's head back.

243
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:13,140
I've figured out...

244
00:27:13,720 --> 00:27:15,100
how to help you.

245
00:28:05,500 --> 00:28:08,460
The new professor is so hardworking.

246
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:12,220
He’s been teaching all day,
yet he's still here practicing.

247
00:28:12,970 --> 00:28:13,620
Geez...

248
00:28:53,650 --> 00:28:55,140
Oh! Professor.

249
00:28:55,490 --> 00:28:56,940
You're staying late today.

250
00:28:57,690 --> 00:28:58,740
I was tutoring a student.

251
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:01,020
I see. Did they already leave?

252
00:29:10,530 --> 00:29:14,900
On my way back.
Caught a ride with a neighbor.

253
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:16,140
Yes, she just left.

254
00:29:17,090 --> 00:29:18,500
No wonder I didn’t see anyone.

255
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:21,180
By the way, don't you need to
pick up your child?

256
00:29:31,340 --> 00:29:34,460
It's fine to forget about me,
but you forget our child!

257
00:29:34,930 --> 00:29:38,260
Thank goodness her teacher stayed.

258
00:29:39,490 --> 00:29:40,620
I'm sorry.

259
00:29:40,970 --> 00:29:43,660
I really was caught up tutoring.

260
00:29:44,210 --> 00:29:46,620
Remember that girl I hit?

261
00:29:46,850 --> 00:29:48,940
I feel really sorry for her.

262
00:29:49,130 --> 00:29:50,500
She’s from such a poor family.

263
00:29:50,650 --> 00:29:52,420
She doesn't even have a fan,

264
00:29:52,570 --> 00:29:55,940
let alone a TV or a computer.

265
00:30:01,970 --> 00:30:04,340
Did you really need to go to her house?

266
00:30:06,560 --> 00:30:10,100
She’s an adult. She should manage.

267
00:30:10,450 --> 00:30:13,780
She could borrow one
or use the university computers.

268
00:30:14,250 --> 00:30:16,420
Besides, you're not her advisor.

269
00:30:16,540 --> 00:30:18,500
You don't need to listen to
all her problems.

270
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:22,220
You have your own family to care for.

271
00:30:35,010 --> 00:30:36,140
I didn't do it!

272
00:30:40,650 --> 00:30:42,420
I really did not.

273
00:30:45,850 --> 00:30:46,780
Honey!

274
00:30:48,490 --> 00:30:49,220
Be careful!

275
00:30:50,580 --> 00:30:51,420
Thep,

276
00:30:51,530 --> 00:30:53,340
I really didn't do it.

277
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:56,020
If you're tired, just get some rest.

278
00:30:56,610 --> 00:30:58,180
I'll put her to bed.

279
00:31:00,370 --> 00:31:01,580
Thep!

280
00:31:02,050 --> 00:31:03,660
Thep, listen to me.

281
00:31:03,780 --> 00:31:05,700
I swear I didn't do it.

282
00:31:05,870 --> 00:31:09,460
It just fell.
I didn't even touch it.

283
00:31:14,050 --> 00:31:15,260
We'll talk later.

284
00:31:53,130 --> 00:31:53,940
Ah!

285
00:32:57,050 --> 00:32:59,100
Thep, there's something here...

286
00:33:00,450 --> 00:33:01,420
what's going on?

287
00:33:03,840 --> 00:33:05,460
What is it, Mommy?

288
00:33:22,450 --> 00:33:23,380
Thep

289
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:26,020
I think...

290
00:33:26,490 --> 00:33:28,300
this house is haunted.

291
00:33:41,450 --> 00:33:42,860
Should we see a doctor?

292
00:33:45,170 --> 00:33:46,100
Thep.

293
00:33:46,290 --> 00:33:48,140
It's not depression.

294
00:33:48,260 --> 00:33:49,780
And I'm much better now.

295
00:33:49,940 --> 00:33:51,620
I really saw it.

296
00:33:51,930 --> 00:33:55,740
I’ve suspected it for a while,
and today confirmed it.

297
00:33:57,680 --> 00:33:58,980
If it's really haunted,

298
00:33:59,770 --> 00:34:01,220
then why haven't I seen anything?

299
00:34:03,850 --> 00:34:06,220
I guess not everyone can see them.

300
00:34:12,530 --> 00:34:13,340
Ploy,

301
00:34:15,210 --> 00:34:17,060
the reason I moved to work here...

302
00:34:19,090 --> 00:34:21,420
was to get you into a new environment.

303
00:34:21,570 --> 00:34:23,380
I wanted you to be happier.

304
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:26,340
If you're being like this,

305
00:34:26,770 --> 00:34:28,500
then it was all for nothing.

306
00:34:31,010 --> 00:34:33,580
But we don't have to live here.

307
00:34:34,050 --> 00:34:36,140
We can just leave it for the workers.

308
00:34:36,650 --> 00:34:40,340
So we pay extra for no reason at all?

309
00:34:43,530 --> 00:34:44,460
Ploy

310
00:34:47,690 --> 00:34:48,540
Ploy,

311
00:34:50,170 --> 00:34:51,460
let's just go see a doctor.

312
00:34:52,330 --> 00:34:53,780
I think it will help you.

313
00:35:28,570 --> 00:35:30,460
This is the only copy we found.

314
00:35:31,770 --> 00:35:33,460
Well, may I ask...

315
00:35:39,410 --> 00:35:40,860
Can you see me, Khem?

316
00:35:43,090 --> 00:35:43,900
Khem?

317
00:35:45,690 --> 00:35:47,300
We've met before, right?

318
00:35:47,810 --> 00:35:49,340
Who are you talking to?

319
00:35:50,280 --> 00:35:50,940
Oh,

320
00:35:51,450 --> 00:35:52,780
I was just talking to her...

321
00:35:54,690 --> 00:35:55,220
Wait.

322
00:35:58,160 --> 00:35:59,620
What woman?

323
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:02,020
There's no one else here.

324
00:36:05,740 --> 00:36:07,100
I was only joking.

325
00:36:08,210 --> 00:36:08,780
Yeah.

326
00:36:08,930 --> 00:36:09,940
You're joking?

327
00:36:10,130 --> 00:36:11,340
- Yes.
- What a relief.

328
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:12,860
I thought you saw a ghost.

329
00:36:13,010 --> 00:36:14,660
I'm on this shift all alone.

330
00:36:14,850 --> 00:36:15,500
Right.

331
00:36:19,640 --> 00:36:20,580
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

332
00:37:20,450 --> 00:37:22,540
You want to know
what happened, don't you?

333
00:38:06,090 --> 00:38:07,220
What are you cooking?

334
00:38:08,450 --> 00:38:09,860
Chicken curry with rice.

335
00:38:09,980 --> 00:38:11,500
It's for the Lady to taste.

336
00:38:13,080 --> 00:38:14,740
Anyone who tastes your curry...

337
00:38:14,890 --> 00:38:17,580
will surely fall in love with it.

338
00:38:21,090 --> 00:38:22,900
She can be a bit snobbish,

339
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:25,300
but she's not heartless.

340
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:28,300
Just keep her happy,
and you'll win her over.

341
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:36,780
Bu-nga,

342
00:38:36,930 --> 00:38:39,140
make sure you don't add eggs.
She's allergic.

343
00:38:39,450 --> 00:38:41,660
What? People can be allergic to eggs?

344
00:38:42,810 --> 00:38:43,940
I'm not entirely sure.

345
00:38:44,640 --> 00:38:47,340
But when she accidentally eats them,

346
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:48,780
she gets terribly ill.

347
00:38:49,570 --> 00:38:50,900
I'm glad you told me.

348
00:39:00,210 --> 00:39:01,340
Are you hungry?

349
00:39:01,550 --> 00:39:02,780
Have you eaten?

350
00:39:03,290 --> 00:39:03,900
No.

351
00:39:04,130 --> 00:39:06,340
I’m going shopping for Lady Mok.

352
00:39:06,530 --> 00:39:07,700
Do you need anything?

353
00:39:09,720 --> 00:39:11,300
Can you get me some nutmeg?

354
00:39:11,570 --> 00:39:12,860
I've been craving it for days.

355
00:39:13,640 --> 00:39:14,380
Sure.

356
00:39:44,330 --> 00:39:45,380
Smells amazing.

357
00:39:46,410 --> 00:39:49,500
Are you making chicken curry?

358
00:39:49,930 --> 00:39:50,660
Yes.

359
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:53,820
I had it once at the Muslim market.

360
00:39:54,090 --> 00:39:55,500
I absolutely loved it.

361
00:39:56,160 --> 00:39:58,420
I’m making some for you, too.

362
00:39:59,020 --> 00:40:01,660
Let me help so we can finish sooner.

363
00:40:02,170 --> 00:40:02,860
Sure.

364
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:05,460
Should I marinate the chicken?

365
00:40:05,880 --> 00:40:08,540
The Lady isn't fond of chicken breast.

366
00:40:08,700 --> 00:40:10,340
She says it's too dry.

367
00:40:11,170 --> 00:40:13,500
Really?
Then let's marinate it.

368
00:40:13,890 --> 00:40:14,540
Okay.

369
00:40:46,330 --> 00:40:48,180
Here's the chicken curry.

370
00:40:49,530 --> 00:40:51,220
I wanted you to try it.

371
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:09,260
Is this a Muslim recipe?

372
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:12,700
I heard your mother was Muslim.

373
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:15,700
My grandfather was Malay,

374
00:41:16,010 --> 00:41:16,860
and...

375
00:41:17,170 --> 00:41:18,740
my grandmother was Chinese.

376
00:41:20,710 --> 00:41:22,740
Quite a mix, isn't it?

377
00:42:15,600 --> 00:42:16,420
So,

378
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:20,620
don't just sit around.
Go back to work.

379
00:42:21,680 --> 00:42:22,580
Yes, ma'am.

380
00:42:42,080 --> 00:42:43,340
Did something bite you?

381
00:42:43,570 --> 00:42:44,500
I don't know.

382
00:42:44,730 --> 00:42:46,060
- Oh my god!
- I'm suddenly itching.

383
00:42:46,450 --> 00:42:47,900
You have a rash.

384
00:42:57,450 --> 00:42:58,260
Bu-nga!

385
00:42:58,490 --> 00:43:00,540
- Did you put eggs in this?
- No.

386
00:43:01,690 --> 00:43:03,460
- I didn't.
- You little tramp!

387
00:43:04,250 --> 00:43:04,860
Hey!

388
00:43:05,050 --> 00:43:06,620
- Get off me, Khem!
- Auntie!

389
00:43:06,880 --> 00:43:07,900
What is it?

390
00:43:08,450 --> 00:43:11,060
- She is pregnant!
- I know that!

391
00:43:14,500 --> 00:43:15,500
What's going on here?

392
00:43:15,780 --> 00:43:16,540
Mok!

393
00:43:17,290 --> 00:43:18,740
Mok, please help me.

394
00:43:18,970 --> 00:43:21,180
They're accusing me of feeding her eggs.

395
00:43:21,490 --> 00:43:22,820
I didn't do it.

396
00:43:24,010 --> 00:43:25,100
I can vouch for her.

397
00:43:25,490 --> 00:43:26,700
I warned her myself.

398
00:43:26,970 --> 00:43:28,020
That's enough!

399
00:43:29,650 --> 00:43:30,780
Sister,

400
00:43:31,370 --> 00:43:32,380
how are you feeling?

401
00:43:33,340 --> 00:43:37,660
She’s covered in hives.
Even on her neck!

402
00:43:38,050 --> 00:43:38,940
Phon

403
00:43:39,170 --> 00:43:40,220
Go fetch the doctor! Hurry!

404
00:43:40,330 --> 00:43:41,100
Right away.

405
00:43:44,720 --> 00:43:45,740
How are you feeling?

406
00:44:06,610 --> 00:44:08,660
I didn't add a single drop of egg.

407
00:44:11,760 --> 00:44:12,980
You said...

408
00:44:13,240 --> 00:44:15,060
Lady Mok helped you, right?

409
00:44:18,480 --> 00:44:21,140
Let me help so we can finish sooner.

410
00:44:21,610 --> 00:44:22,260
Sure.

411
00:44:22,730 --> 00:44:24,300
Should I marinate the chicken?

412
00:44:24,690 --> 00:44:27,340
The Lady isn't fond of chicken breast.

413
00:44:27,530 --> 00:44:29,260
She says it's too dry.

414
00:44:29,970 --> 00:44:32,260
Really?
Then let's marinate it.

415
00:44:32,680 --> 00:44:33,300
Okay.

416
00:44:35,610 --> 00:44:37,060
Mok would never do that.

417
00:44:40,720 --> 00:44:41,940
But if it were Phon...

418
00:44:42,960 --> 00:44:44,500
I wouldn't be surprised.

419
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:52,140
Maybe she already had a rash...

420
00:44:53,360 --> 00:44:55,940
and faked it just to frame you.

421
00:45:01,130 --> 00:45:03,660
So they could get me kicked out?

422
00:45:13,970 --> 00:45:14,780
In that case...

423
00:45:15,370 --> 00:45:16,620
no matter what happens...

424
00:45:19,490 --> 00:45:21,100
I'll stay and wait for Thep.

425
00:45:39,560 --> 00:45:42,700
Thank you for your time, Doctor.

426
00:45:43,130 --> 00:45:45,060
Don't mention it. I'll take my leave.

427
00:45:48,450 --> 00:45:50,140
- Phon
- Yes?

428
00:45:50,360 --> 00:45:51,620
See the doctor out.

429
00:45:51,930 --> 00:45:52,740
Yes.

430
00:45:53,730 --> 00:45:55,780
- I'll be right back.
- Alright.

431
00:45:57,690 --> 00:45:58,620
Right this way.

432
00:46:07,490 --> 00:46:10,100
What are you going to do
about Bu-nga?

433
00:46:13,480 --> 00:46:15,860
I don't have to tell you everything.

434
00:46:36,570 --> 00:46:39,340
My dearest Bu-nga,

435
00:46:40,970 --> 00:46:42,140
I'm sorry...

436
00:46:42,450 --> 00:46:45,060
for not writing the moment I arrived.

437
00:46:45,800 --> 00:46:47,940
I've been very busy.

438
00:46:48,850 --> 00:46:51,540
I miss you with every breath.

439
00:47:01,770 --> 00:47:02,860
Are you still awake?

440
00:47:03,640 --> 00:47:04,500
Yes.

441
00:47:05,210 --> 00:47:06,180
What are you doing?

442
00:47:07,490 --> 00:47:10,100
Writing to Mother and Bu-nga.

443
00:47:13,850 --> 00:47:15,100
Get some sleep when you're finished.

444
00:47:15,570 --> 00:47:17,460
We meet the Governor early tomorrow.

445
00:47:18,570 --> 00:47:19,300
Understood.

446
00:48:06,050 --> 00:48:07,300
Turn right up ahead.

447
00:48:07,740 --> 00:48:08,420
By the way...

448
00:48:09,010 --> 00:48:10,460
whose house are we visiting?

449
00:48:11,170 --> 00:48:12,620
My friend's. Luang Wiset.

450
00:48:13,250 --> 00:48:14,220
Don't you remember?

451
00:48:14,450 --> 00:48:18,460
Your mother insisted these gifts
were for him and his wife.

452
00:48:29,400 --> 00:48:30,860
Thank you so much, my friend.

453
00:48:31,050 --> 00:48:34,620
You don't need to bring gifts next time.

454
00:48:34,970 --> 00:48:38,380
Just seeing you makes me happy.

455
00:48:39,170 --> 00:48:40,180
Oh, please.

456
00:48:40,330 --> 00:48:41,900
Don't be so formal.

457
00:48:42,250 --> 00:48:43,020
Look.

458
00:48:43,290 --> 00:48:45,420
Dried fish and shrimp.

459
00:48:46,210 --> 00:48:49,660
Lady Duangkhae saw to it herself.

460
00:48:50,290 --> 00:48:51,460
And that's velvet tamarind.

461
00:48:51,650 --> 00:48:54,100
It’s delicious and very clean.

462
00:48:56,810 --> 00:48:59,980
My niece will love this.

463
00:49:00,210 --> 00:49:02,460
- She loves eating--
- Cooking.

464
00:49:05,570 --> 00:49:08,580
She absolutely loves cooking.

465
00:49:11,680 --> 00:49:12,260
I see.

466
00:49:12,410 --> 00:49:13,740
She must be in the kitchen now.

467
00:49:13,890 --> 00:49:15,140
Oh, not at all.

468
00:49:15,410 --> 00:49:16,860
She's still at school.

469
00:49:17,760 --> 00:49:20,660
Besides being good at housework,

470
00:49:20,930 --> 00:49:22,700
she's also very smart.

471
00:49:24,360 --> 00:49:25,460
As they say,

472
00:49:25,640 --> 00:49:27,420
her father was a nobleman.

473
00:49:28,880 --> 00:49:30,340
But sadly,

474
00:49:30,570 --> 00:49:32,380
her parents died young.

475
00:49:33,040 --> 00:49:34,660
So she was orphaned.

476
00:49:39,010 --> 00:49:40,060
Excuse me.

477
00:49:40,680 --> 00:49:42,980
I just remembered
I need to mail a letter.

478
00:49:43,280 --> 00:49:44,820
Is there a mailbox around here?

479
00:49:45,370 --> 00:49:46,540
Um...

480
00:49:47,130 --> 00:49:48,460
Leave the house,

481
00:49:49,010 --> 00:49:51,580
turn left, and keep walking along the fence.

482
00:49:51,800 --> 00:49:54,540
It's just a few houses down.

483
00:49:54,770 --> 00:49:55,940
Thank you so much.

484
00:49:58,220 --> 00:49:59,580
Hurry back.

485
00:49:59,730 --> 00:50:01,340
I made bananas in coconut milk.

486
00:50:01,530 --> 00:50:02,300
Will do.

487
00:50:14,450 --> 00:50:16,500
How many today?

488
00:50:17,970 --> 00:50:21,180
I studied hard today. I'll take ten.

489
00:50:21,300 --> 00:50:22,340
You got it.

490
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:26,860
Want a snack?

491
00:50:27,970 --> 00:50:29,300
Hello there.

492
00:50:29,460 --> 00:50:30,900
Are you new here?

493
00:50:31,160 --> 00:50:32,380
I haven't seen you around.

494
00:50:35,050 --> 00:50:35,820
You.

495
00:51:17,930 --> 00:51:20,340
May you be loved and cherished.

496
00:51:25,040 --> 00:51:26,140
Is this...

497
00:51:26,290 --> 00:51:29,300
Bu-nga, how dare you steal
Lady Mok's bracelet?

498
00:51:29,460 --> 00:51:31,140
- I...
- Did you find it?

499
00:51:31,480 --> 00:51:32,500
Right here.

500
00:51:34,210 --> 00:51:36,100
- But, I...
- It's always you!

501
00:51:36,810 --> 00:51:38,540
First, you tried to kill the Lady.

502
00:51:38,770 --> 00:51:40,500
Now you steal from Lady Mok.

503
00:51:40,690 --> 00:51:42,220
You’re nothing but a born thief.

504
00:51:42,410 --> 00:51:44,060
I really didn't do it.

505
00:51:45,360 --> 00:51:47,100
You dare suspect me?

506
00:51:47,450 --> 00:51:49,660
Because you think
I’m a wicked woman.

507
00:51:50,090 --> 00:51:52,660
You do believe that
this baby isn't your grandchild.

508
00:51:52,890 --> 00:51:54,700
You’re just trying to get rid of me.

509
00:51:55,090 --> 00:51:56,100
Lock her up.

510
00:51:56,330 --> 00:51:57,980
Don't let her see the light of day.

511
00:51:58,130 --> 00:52:00,420
- She's Thep's wife!
- Shut it, Khem!

512
00:52:00,970 --> 00:52:03,620
Otherwise, you’ll be punished as well.

513
00:52:05,250 --> 00:52:07,420
Get her out of my sight.

514
00:52:08,600 --> 00:52:09,300
Go!

515
00:52:10,890 --> 00:52:13,540
- She's a human being.
- Shall we send her away?

516
00:52:13,810 --> 00:52:14,780
I'm not going back.

517
00:52:15,810 --> 00:52:17,660
I'll wait for Thep here.

518
00:52:26,530 --> 00:52:27,940
I can remember my past lives, right?

519
00:52:28,060 --> 00:52:29,860
If you really can,

520
00:52:31,450 --> 00:52:32,940
you must have seen it all.

521
00:52:33,170 --> 00:52:35,260
I feel like someone else
is in the house.

522
00:52:35,850 --> 00:52:37,620
Someone... not human.

523
00:52:38,610 --> 00:52:40,260
Put these on the front door,

524
00:52:40,530 --> 00:52:42,820
the back door, and the bedroom.

525
00:52:43,330 --> 00:52:44,140
Understood.

526
00:52:45,770 --> 00:52:48,180
What's that, Dad?

527
00:52:56,130 --> 00:52:57,820
Bu-nga is still waiting for Thep.

528
00:53:01,370 --> 00:53:03,020
Hey, Bu-nga!

529
00:53:07,620 --> 00:53:09,180
If death were the end,

530
00:53:09,330 --> 00:53:11,020
who would pay me back?

531
00:53:11,210 --> 00:53:13,100
Stay out of this!
